# Design tokens

All color must come from `src/styles/tokens.css` (and the JS mirror `src/styles/tokens.js`).

Allowed values only:

- Background (off-white): `#F8F8F5` → `var(--color-background)`
- Surface (white): `#FFFFFF` → `var(--color-surface)`
- Primary (near-black): `#1A1A1A` → `var(--color-primary)`
- Emergency Red: `#D62828` → `var(--color-emergency)`
- Deep Red: `#9D0208` → `var(--color-emergency-deep)`
- Muted: `#5C5C5C` → `var(--color-muted)`
- Border: `#E8E8E2` → `var(--color-border)`

## Rules

- Do not introduce new hex, rgb, rgba, hsl, or named CSS colors in components, pages, or extra stylesheets.
- Do not use social-network brand colors, Bootstrap blues, or the old green NGO palette (`#2c8b73`, etc.).
- Hover / active / focus use Emergency Red or Deep Red. Body text uses Primary. Secondary text uses Muted. Dividers use Border.
- Red may be used as a full section surface (impact bands, CTAs). Deep red is for hover and dark red sections.
- Font Awesome is for UI controls (search, play, menu, close, phone, mail). Historical identities use NewspaperMark, OrganizationMark, or the original photograph — never a generic newspaper / trophy / YouTube icon.
- Success states stay in this system (Primary or Emergency). Never add green, purple, or terracotta.
- If a new token is truly required, add it to `tokens.css` and `tokens.js` first, then use the variable.
- Use `src/components/RedLine/RedLine.jsx` for the road / heartbeat journey mark.
